<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width">
  <title>My Media Adventure</title>
</head>

<body>

  <center>

    <h1>My Media Adventure Webpage</h1>

    <p>
      Welcome to my exciting media adventure! Here, you can explore amazing places,
      listen to music, watch a video, and enjoy an interactive game.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h2>Underwater Adventure Gallery</h2>

    <p>
      These images show the amazing creatures and beautiful places I discovered
      during my underwater adventure.
    </p>

    <img src="ocean.png" alt="A beautiful ocean" width="300" height="300">
    <img src="dolphin.png" alt="A dolphin swimming in the ocean" width="300" height="300">
    <img src="fish.png" alt="Colourful fish underwater" width="300" height="300">

    <hr>

    <h2>Ocean Beats Party</h2>

    <p>
      Listen to some relaxing music while enjoying an underwater video.
    </p>

    <audio controls loop>
      <source src="oceanmusic.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
      Your browser does not support the audio tag.
    </audio>

    <br><br>

    <video width="500" height="350" controls poster="oceanposter.png" loop>
      <source src="oceanvideo.mp4" type="video/mp4">
      Your browser does not support the video tag.
    </video>

    <hr>

    <h2>Adventure Game Zone</h2>

    <p>
      Play this fun Scratch game and see if you can complete the adventure!
    </p>

    <iframe 
      src="https://scratch.mit.edu/projects/60917032/embed"
      allowtransparency="true"
      width="500"
      height="400"
      frameborder="0"
      scrolling="no"
      allowfullscreen>
    </iframe>

    <hr>

    <h2>Adventure Complete!</h2>

    <p>
      I used image, audio, video, and iframe tags to create my own interactive
      media adventure webpage.
    </p>

  </center>

</body>

</html>